abstract: >-
  A verification-gated Claude Code template for academic research in
  bioenergy and circular biorefinery science — biomass pyrolysis and
  gasification, hydrothermal conversion, biochar, hydrogen production,
  microbial conversion, waste valorization, and life-cycle / techno-economic
  assessment. Supports manuscripts, research proposals, experimental data
  analysis (R and Python), literature reviews, reports, and presentations.
  Fan-out review fleets with hallucination gates, numeric-claim
  reproducibility audits against code, and an enforcing pre-commit quality
  gate. This is a customized fork, maintained by Gözde Duman Taç, of the
  original Claude Code Academic Workflow template created by Pedro H. C.
  Sant'Anna (see `references` below) for Econ 730: Causal Panel Data at
  Emory University; the underlying orchestration, review, and quality-gate
  infrastructure is retained, with domain-specific tooling retargeted for
  bioenergy research.
references:
